Subject: [PATCH] Bound and observe DoltLite HTTP session transfers
Base: DoltLite v0.50.15 with local patches 0001-0008 applied

This is a regenerated net patch from the state after DoltLite patches 0001-0008.
Its source was produced by applying the former 0009-0016 series in order, then
adding only the C comments below. On an upstream refresh, retain every numbered
intent below when regenerating this patch; do not edit the pristine vendored
amalgamation or remote sidecars.

Retained intent from the former DoltLite patches:
- 0009: Keep public RemoteServer limits at 64 MiB per chunk and 128 MiB per
  request. A session-owned numeric IPv4 loopback server may accept bodies up to
  the native signed-int bound; a single Prolly chunk stays 24 bytes below it for
  hash and length framing. Permit slow body progress for this same-process
  loopback path while ordinary servers retain their request limits.
- 0010: Make HTTP timeouts inactivity limits refreshed by successful reads and
  writes. Keep TCP connect and TLS handshake bounded at 30 seconds and update
  the staged TLS sidecar to match DoltliteConn's layout.
- 0011: Add request-local http_idle_timeout_ms, capped at five minutes and
  taking precedence over DOLTLITE_HTTP_TIMEOUT_MS; keep the environment value
  as the default override.
- 0012: Preserve fixed HTTP transport phase and configured idle-timeout context
  for socket and response failures without leaking URLs, headers, credentials,
  provider bodies, or mislabeling arbitrary socket errors as timeouts. Preserve
  SQLite result codes and retry behavior.
- 0013: Allow timeout value zero only for clear HTTP URLs with a numeric IPv4
  literal in 127/8. URI-backed session loopback RemoteServers use it while
  ordinary remotes and TLS session URLs retain their configured idle timeout.
- 0014: Add an opt-in per-connection Rust callback for logical Dolt push chunk
  progress, without changing public SQL or HTTP behavior. Plan the reachable,
  destination-missing chunks before transfer and retain hashes and lengths, not
  payloads. Count synchronous writes on success and HTTP writes only after the
  full batch succeeds.
- 0015: Retry oversized /get-chunks responses as smaller hash ranges after HTTP
  413 or the fixed 128 MiB response bound, preserve output order, and keep a
  single overlarge chunk an error.
- 0016: Decode strict HTTP/1.1 chunked responses without Content-Length. Validate
  bounded extensions and trailers, cap encoded and decoded bodies at 128 MiB,
  and stop when the final chunk arrives even on a keepalive connection.

Cross-tree dependencies: the RemoteServer session-loopback option is consumed
by the rusqdoltlite session-owned server integration. The callback here feeds
logical chunk progress; CBS patch 0017 separately reports physical block
progress, authorization refresh, integrity checks, and storage failures. The
build applies this patch to staged copies of doltlite.c and the remote C
sidecars; keep those vendored upstream files pristine.

